# doomcode colours: ~/.config/doomcode/theme
#
# Everything below is commented out: these are doom-light's built-in
# colours, for reference. Uncomment a line and change it to override that
# colour in whatever palette is in use (choose the palette in the config
# file).
#   palette NAME                       base palette (the config file's palette wins)
#   style NAME fg=#rrggbb bg=#rrggbb line=#rrggbb underline|nounderline
#   style NAME -                       draw NAME as plain text
#   text.back #rrggbb [mix #rrggbb]    window colours (slots: tag.* text.* with
#                                      back high bord text htext tick;
#                                      ui.modbutton ui.colbutton ui.but2 ui.but3)
# Colours are #rgb, #rrggbb or #rrggbbaa. "Theme" prints the styles in
# effect; after a change: Theme reload (window colours: restart).
# How the doomcode palettes are chosen: docs/10-theme-style-guide.md.

# palette doom-light

# style comment      fg=#646f61
# style constant     fg=#86497f
# style diff.add     bg=#dff0d8
# style diff.change  bg=#f4ebc8
# style diff.del     bg=#f6dcd8
# style emphasis     fg=#5c4a86
# style error        bg=#f6dcd8 underline line=#b5524a
# style function     fg=#3f5c94
# style heading      fg=#35539a
# style hint         bg=#e0edda underline line=#4e8a4e
# style info         bg=#dce7f3 underline line=#3f6aa8
# style keyword      fg=#35539a
# style link         fg=#3468b0 underline
# style match        bg=#f0de9a
# style number       fg=#7a4c98
# style preproc      fg=#7d6420
# style string       fg=#94552b
# style type         fg=#2e716f
# style warning      bg=#f4ebc8 underline line=#a07a20
